b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING reposed;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays whose bounds are computed at run time (5.2.4.2), and the for statement with a step-until element over the subscripts of an array (4.6, and its example in 4.6.1), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), a sequence as an integer array with a length (systems file, Values), and the observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS none. n is the instance's size, from the instance line, and the sequence is the one of 1 to n that the problem names;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P13e, native. The algorithm: the sequence of 1 to n is built in the integer array s[1:n] by a for statement, s[i] := i, and is held there until the answer is given. Then a second for statement adds its elements, in order, to total, which begins at 0. Each loop takes n steps of the for statement, so the work is linear in n, and the store is the n elements of s. The problem's unknown k is called total here, since k names the stage number;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, size;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line, and the one message, which poses stage 1;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  code := read; k := read;
  size := i̲f̲ n < 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ n;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ total, built, added;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ s[1:size];

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
      d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
      i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ num;

  built := added := 0;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ build the sequence of 1 to n;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ n d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ s[i] := i; built := built + 1 e̲n̲d̲;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ sum it;
  total := 0;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ n d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ total := total + s[i]; added := added + 1 e̲n̲d̲;

  PRINTTEXT(`[answer]k = '); num(total); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the elements built and added, and the store held after the answer;
  PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`native: the sequence made in the vector s of n elements by one loop, and summed by a second loop'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`elements held after the answer: '); num(n); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, the vector s, kept as long as the program runs'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[bind k]'); num(total); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`elements built: '); num(built); PRINTTEXT(`, elements added: '); num(added); NLCR;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
